  "conclusion": "Slow memory does learn the repeated stable correction, but the legacy fixed-radius fast search can erase that advantage near the solution. A conventional distance-scaled trust region plus one-measurement accept/reject handoff converts the learned prior into large future probe savings. Ordinary EMA and Kalman-style estimators are sufficient; correct context addressing is essential."
